  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal, by reason of siting, mass and design, would be an undesirable addition which would create a new\r\ndiscordant frontage along a section of Sylvan Avenue which is characterised by its openness and would appear at\r\nodds within the rear garden setting. As such, it fails to respect or reflect the character of the host dwelling, local area\r\nand street scene along Sylvan Avenue, causing harm to each of these. The proposal thus fails to accord with the\r\nfollowing policies which seek to ensure development proposals are well designed, suitable for the site and local\r\ncontext, and respect and reflect the existing character: National Planning Policy Framework (December,\r\n2023)\r\nPolicies D3, D4 and D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)\r\nPolicy CP3 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010)\r\nPolicies BP8 and BP11 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document\r\n(DPD) (March 2011)\r\nPolicies SP2, DMD1 and DMD6 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan:\r\n(Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposal, by reason of siting, scale and design, would be an undesirable addition which would cause an\r\nunacceptable loss of daylight and an unacceptable overbearing impact to neighbouring dwellings.\r\nThis would result in a harmful impact to the amenity currently enjoyed by neighbouring occupiers. As such, it fails to\r\nprotect residential amenity and constitutes un-neighbourly development. The proposal thus fails to accord with the\r\nfollowing policies which seek to ensure that development proposals protect residential amenity: National Planning Policy Framework (December,\r\n2023) Part D of Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)\r\nPolicies BP8 and BP11 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document\r\n(DPD) (March 2011)\r\nSection 4.2 of the Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)\r\nPolicies DMD1 and DMD6 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19\r\nSubmission Version, December 2021)",
    "In the absence of further information, the proposal is considered likely to provide insufficient natural daylight, sunlight and ventilation, to the detriment of the living conditions of future occupiers. The proposal thus fails to accord with the following policies which seek to ensure\r\ndevelopment proposals protect residential amenity and provide a suitable quality of accommodation: National Planning Policy Framework (December,\r\n2023)\r\nPolicy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)\r\nPolicies BP8 and BP11 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document\r\n(DPD) (March 2011)\r\nPolicies DMD1 and DMD6 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19\r\nSubmission Version, December 2021)&nbsp;Housing Design Standards London Plan Guidance (GLA, June 2023)"
  ],
